{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואש מתלקחת", :translit "v'eish mitlakahat", :gloss "and fire taking hold"} {:he "ואש מתלקחת ונוגה לו סביב", :translit "v'eish mitlakahat v'nogah lo saviv", :gloss "and fire taking hold and its glow around him"} {:he "בתוך הברד היה האש", :translit "b'toch habarad hayah ha'eish", :gloss "within the hail was the fire"} {:he "ויוצא ממנו נצוצות ומאורים", :translit "v'yotze mimenu nitzotzot um'orim", :gloss "and from it went out sparks and lights"} {:he "ונוגה לו סביב", :translit "v'nogah lo saviv", :gloss "and its glow around him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואש מתלקחת" "ואש מתלקחת ונוגה לו סביב"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase ואש מתלקחת ונוגה לו סביב appears in Ezekiel 1:4 as part of the prophet's vision of the divine chariot, describing fiery brightness surrounding the storm cloud. Ba'al HaTurim reads this parallel phrase back into Exodus: just as Ezekiel 1:4 describes fire and radiance within a cloud, so in the seventh plague the hail contained fire, producing sparks and illumination. He thus links the theophanic imagery of Ezekiel 1:4 to the plague narrative of Exodus 9:24.", :sources ["Ezekiel 1:4" "Exodus 9:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואש מתלקחת" "ואש מתלקחת ונוגה לו סביב"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ואש מתלקחת", :refs ["Exodus 9:24" "Ezekiel 1:4"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ואש מתלקחת ונוגה לו סביב", :refs ["Ezekiel 1:4"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:38.277422380Z", :model "glm-5.2"}